Validated 1 entities; 0 errors, 0 gaps
Body: 0 words (Context 0, Alternatives 0, Decision 0, Consequences 0, Prevents 0)
Lens alternatives: A real alternative, not a strawman
  A decision with one option on the table is a description, not a decision. Name
  what else was genuinely considered and what it would have cost. If there was only
  ever one option, say that and say why — that is a constraint, and it belongs in
  Context.
Lens consequences: The cost, not only the benefit
  Consequences that are all upside means the tradeoff has not been found yet. What
  got harder? What can no longer be done cheaply? A reader six months from now is
  here because something is painful and they want to know whether this record
  predicted it.
Lens reversal: What would reverse this
  Name the observation that would make this the wrong call. Without it, nobody
  knows when to open a superseding record — and `supersedes` is the edge that makes
  the history readable.
Lens rule: A rule needs a requirement
  If this decision creates something the system must always or never do, that is a
  `requirement`, not a paragraph here. Add it and link it — `affects` carries the
  blast radius, and a rule buried in an ADR body is a rule nothing can check.
Lens proposed: Still proposed
  This record is not decided yet. Confirm the Decision section reads as the
  proposal it is, and that whoever has to accept or reject it can tell what they
  are being asked.
